 **Edge Cases and Pitfalls:**
-*   **Aliasing:** Occurs because pixel value should be defined by integration along a cone, not just ray accumulation. Addressed by mipmapping and cone tracing [S4, unofficial].
-*   **Popping:** Discrete mipmap levels can cause popping. Addressed by smooth transitions and continuous adaptation [S4, unofficial].
-*   **Memory Budget:** The method respects limited GPU memory by streaming, but out-of-core rendering is essential for vast worlds [S6, unofficial].
+*   **Aliasing:** Caused by defining pixel value by ray accumulation rather than cone integration. Addressed by mipmapping and cone tracing [S4, unofficial].
+*   **Memory Limits:** Out-of-core rendering is essential for vast worlds; the method relies on the cache to manage this [S6, unofficial].
+*   **Procedural Noise:** Reusing noise computation requires careful management of cache levels to ensure $F(\text{level } N)$ correctly sums octaves [S1, unofficial].
 
